ENGLISH (FRANCAIS voir plus bas)
KhiCAS, free (GPL3) computer algebra system for TI nspire CX (II) calculators, OS version 4.5.3/5.2, with support for multi-precision floats and interval arithmetic.
For black and white nspire, please try
http://www-fourier.ujf-grenoble.fr/public_html/calc/khicasbw.zip

You must install ndless to run KhiCAS, either the version provided here or see
instructions on ndless.me or tiplanet.org 
Then send luagiac.luax.tns and khicaslua.tns to your calculator. 
Then from Home, My Documents, select khicaslua and press Enter.
You can run all Xcas commands from here, for example
a:=partfrac(1/(x^4-1))
normal(a)
factor(a)
ifactor(2^128+1)
evalf(pi,30)
For help on a command, type ? then the commandname (from menu or keyboard)

Important note: if the luagiac module fails to load, make sure
ndless is active, run ndless_installer if it is not and try again.

